Hello Mesa Electrical Field Services,

Please carry out work order WO-1 on INV-3 (reseat_comms_card).

Steps, in order:
  1. Open AC disconnect upstream of INV-3 (breaker 52-In)
  2. Verify zero energy with calibrated tester on AC input to INV-3
  3. Apply lockout device and tagout to AC disconnect upstream of INV-3
  4. Confirm no residual voltage on INV-3 AC input terminals before work
  5. Verify loss of AC power to INV-3 by checking the circuit breaker and iso=
lating the inverter.
  6. Open the inverter cabinet door and locate the inverter comms card (typic=
ally mounted on the side or rear panel).
  7. Carefully remove the comms card from its slot, ensuring to note orientat=
ion and any locking levers.
  8. Inspect the card slot and card connectors for dust, oxidation, or physic=
al damage.
  9. Reinsert the comms card firmly until it clicks or seats fully, matching =
the original orientation.
  10. Close the cabinet door and restore AC power to the inverter.
  11. Power on the inverter and observe the display for illumination and init=
ialisation.
  12. Ping the inverter's IP address from the SCADA workstation to confirm co=
mms_ping test success.
  13. Monitor the SCADA portal for a telemetry update and verify display read=
ings are live.
  14. If the display remains dark or ping times out, escalate to replace the =
comms card or check cabling.
  15. Restore AC power to INV-3 by closing breaker 52-In
  16. Verify power restoration with operational test of INV-3 comms and displ=
ay

Do not:
  - Do not force the comms card out or push it in at an angle, risking damage=
 to the slot.
  - Do not skip the power isolation step before handling internal components.
  - Do not assume the fault is the cable; always reseat the card first per di=
agnostics.
  - Do not ignore a dark display without checking power and card seating.

We will verify against the plant before closing this order:
  - INV-3 SCADA data_age_min at most 5 and status running
  - INV-3 answers comms_ping (its comms card is back on the network)
  - INV-3 display lit and showing readings in a camera view the verifier pick=
s, not the contractor's photo
  - JEV verdict 'verified' from the registered camera stations and the sensor=
 state
  - SCADA system shows INV-3 telemetry data_age_min less than 5 minutes and s=
tatus 'running'
  - INV-3 responds to comms_ping with successful reply (no timeout)
  - Physical inspection of INV-3 cabinet shows lit, readable display with vis=
ible operational readings

Reply to this email when the work is done.

